{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\ntypedef long long ll;\n\nstruct step {\n    ll val;\n    int cost;\n    bool operator>(const step &c) const {\n        return cost > c.cost;\n    }\n};\n\nunordered_set<ll> visited;\n\nbool wasVisited(ll c) {\n    return visited.find(c) != visited.end();\n}\n\nstep uupper(ll n) {\n    ll res = 0;\n    int i = 0;\n    while (res < n) {\n        res = res * 10 + 1;\n        i++;\n    }\n    return {res, i};\n}\n\nstep upper(ll n) {\n    ll res = 0;\n    int i = 0;\n    while (res * 10 + 1 <= n) {\n        res = res * 10 + 1;\n        i++;\n    }\n    ll resmul = res;\n    int imul = i;\n    while (res < n) {\n        res += resmul;\n        i += imul;\n    }\n    return {res, i};\n}\n\nstep lower(ll n) {\n    ll res = 0;\n    int i = 0;\n    while (res * 10 + 1 <= n) {\n        res = res * 10 + 1;\n        i++;\n    }\n    ll resmul = res;\n    int imul = i;\n    while (res + resmul <= n) {\n        res += resmul;\n        i += imul;\n    }\n    return {res, i};\n}\n\nint main(int argc, char **argv) {\n    ll n;\n    cin >> n;\n    priority_queue<step, vector<step>, greater<step>> pq;\n    pq.push({n, 0});\n    while (pq.top().val != 0) {\n        ll val = pq.top().val;\n        int cost = pq.top().cost;\n        pq.pop();\n        if (wasVisited(val))\n            continue;\n        visited.insert(val);\n        for (step next : {lower(val), upper(val), uupper(val)}) {\n            next.cost += cost;\n            next.val = abs(val - next.val);\n            pq.push(next);\n        }\n    }\n    cout << pq.top().cost << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "```java\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static class Step implements Comparable<Step> {\n        long val;\n        int cost;\n        Step(long val, int cost) {\n            this.val = val;\n            this.cost = cost;\n        }\n        @Override\n        public int compareTo(Step other) {\n            return Integer.compare(this.cost, other.cost);\n        }\n    }\n\n    static HashSet<Long> visited = new HashSet<>();\n\n    static boolean wasVisited(long c) {\n        return visited.contains(c);\n    }\n\n    static Step uupper(long n) {\n        long res = 0;\n        int i = 0;\n        while (res < n) {\n            res = res * 10 + 1;\n            i++;\n        }\n        return new Step(res, i);\n    }\n\n    static Step upper(long n) {\n        long res = 0;\n        int i = 0;\n        while (res * 10 + 1 <= n) {\n            res = res * 10 + 1;\n            i++;\n        }\n        long resmul = res;\n        int imul = i;\n        while (res < n) {\n            res += resmul;\n            i += imul;\n        }\n        return new Step(res, i);\n    }\n\n    static Step lower(long n) {\n        long res = 0;\n        int i = 0;\n        while (res * 10 + 1 <= n) {\n            res = res * 10 + 1;\n            i++;\n        }\n        long resmul = res;\n        int imul = i;\n        while (res + resmul <= n) {\n            res += resmul;\n            i += imul;\n        }\n        return new Step(res, i);\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n        PriorityQueue<Step> pq = new PriorityQueue<>();\n        pq.add(new Step(n, 0));\n        while (pq.peek().val != 0) {\n            Step cur = pq.poll();\n            long val = cur.val;\n            int cost = cur.cost;\n            if (wasVisited(val)) continue;\n            visited.add(val);\n            Step[] nexts = {lower(val), upper(val), uupper(val)};\n            for (Step next : nexts) {\n                next.cost += cost;\n                next.val = Math.abs(val - next.val);\n                pq.add(next);\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(pq.peek().cost);\n    }\n}\n```", "token_logprobs": [-0.5791675448417664, -9.536738616588991e-07, -5.94836674281396e-05, -0.00010382589971413836, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.814624506048858e-05, -0.0024647116661071777, -0.12700322270393372, 0.0, -3.5523738915799186e-05, -0.018228041008114815, -0.003177952254191041, -0.0005268854438327253, -7.247662142617628e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.005234583746641874, 0.0, 0.0, -1.0728830375228426e-06, 0.0, -1.4305104514278355e-06, 0.0, -8.344646857949556e-07, -1.6689160474925302e-05, -5.483612312673358e-06, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, -0.4741198718547821, -0.5759429931640625, -0.0019288521725684404, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -0.3132621645927429, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.0004306104383431375, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -1.680836794548668e-05, -5.8410845667822286e-05, -0.31625092029571533, 0.0, -2.264974000354414e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.011050926521